; einargudni.com — records to import into Cloudflare (DNS > Records > Import)
;
; Covers only what a zone file CAN express. Deliberately NOT here:
;   - apex and www        -> created automatically when you attach the Worker
;                            as a Custom Domain (a zone file cannot express that)
;   - *.einargudni.com    -> the wildcard is being dropped on purpose
;   - MX / SPF / DKIM     -> the zone has none; there is no email to carry over
;
; After importing, set the proxy status by hand — the zone file cannot carry it:
;   posture, nido   -> DNS only  (grey cloud) so Vercel keeps terminating its TLS
;   sologbjor       -> Proxied   (orange cloud)
;
; TTL 300 is deliberate for the transition: it keeps every app migration
; reversible within five minutes. Raise it once things have settled.

$ORIGIN einargudni.com.
$TTL 300

; --- still on Vercel until migrated (phases 08 and 09) ---------------------
posture         300  IN  CNAME  cname.vercel-dns.com.
nido            300  IN  CNAME  cname.vercel-dns.com.

; --- already on Cloudflare Pages ------------------------------------------
sologbjor       300  IN  CNAME  sol-og-bjor.pages.dev.

; --- certificate authority authorisation ----------------------------------
; letsencrypt.org and pki.goog are the two issuers Cloudflare Universal SSL
; uses, so these carry across unchanged and certs provision without edits.
; sectigo.com is retained from the Vercel setup; harmless to keep.
@               300  IN  CAA  0 issue "letsencrypt.org"
@               300  IN  CAA  0 issue "pki.goog"
@               300  IN  CAA  0 issue "sectigo.com"
